# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructions
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Maintainer: replace generic names with names tied to each product. Keep only
# values users commonly change. This scaffold is not runnable as written.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required settings
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Add required connection credentials without usable defaults.
# PRODUCT_TWO_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional settings
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local access by default. Document trusted LAN access before widening it.
# STACK_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# Host port for the first user-facing product.
# PRODUCT_ONE_PORT=8080

# Leave these lines commented to use Docker-managed named volumes.
# Uncomment a line and enter an absolute Linux host path after = only when
# needed. Absolute Linux paths begin with /. Changing a source does not move
# existing data and can change permissions, backup and restore behavior.
# Read the deployment README before changing these values.
# PRODUCT_ONE_DATA_SOURCE=
# PRODUCT_TWO_DATA_SOURCE=

# Optional name for a maintained shared-network extension.
# STACKLAB_NETWORK=stacklab
